CAT = "cpaiscAis"; SEG = "AIS"
Q = [
("What most distinguishes an ERP system from separate departmental systems?",
 "One shared database across functions", ["Separate ledgers for each department", "Batch transfers between modules", "Stand-alone general ledger software"],
 "An ERP system integrates finance, sales, purchasing, HR and other functions on a common database, so a transaction entered once updates every area. Separate ledgers with batch transfers describe the older, unintegrated model."),
("Ordering goods, receiving them, matching vendor invoices and paying vendors belong to which business cycle?",
 "Expenditure cycle", ["Revenue cycle", "Conversion cycle", "Financing cycle"],
 "The expenditure cycle covers purchasing and cash disbursements. The revenue cycle covers sales, shipping, billing and cash collections."),
("Credit approval, shipping and collecting cash from customers are part of which cycle?",
 "Revenue cycle", ["Expenditure cycle", "Production cycle", "Human resources cycle"],
 "The revenue cycle runs from the customer order through shipping, billing and cash collection. Production converts materials into finished goods."),
("A software bot copies data from emailed invoices into the payables system by following fixed rules. This is:",
 "Robotic process automation", ["Electronic data interchange", "Batch processing", "Business process outsourcing"],
 "RPA uses software bots to perform repetitive, rules-based tasks a person would do on screen. EDI is a computer-to-computer exchange of standard documents with no bot keying data."),
("Comparing the purchase order, the receiving report and the vendor invoice before payment is called a:",
 "Three-way match", ["Positive pay check", "Batch control total", "Hash total"],
 "The three-way match confirms that what was ordered was received and billed at the agreed price. Positive pay is a bank service that verifies checks presented."),
("The documented process says a supervisor approves each new vendor, but a walkthrough shows clerks add vendors directly. What has the walkthrough found?",
 "Practice differs from the policy", ["Process improvement already in place", "Approved exception to the policy", "Single data entry error"],
 "Reconciling the observed steps to the documented process is the purpose of a walkthrough. Clerks routinely skipping the approval is a deviation, not a one-off keying mistake."),
("Under the Trust Services Criteria, an edit check that rejects a sales order with a missing customer ID addresses which criterion?",
 "PI1.2, system inputs", ["PI1.3, system processing", "PI1.4, system outputs", "PI1.5, stored items"],
 "PI1.2 covers policies and procedures over system inputs, including controls over completeness and accuracy. PI1.3 covers processing after the data is accepted."),
("A control confirms that reports reach only the intended recipients, complete and accurate. Which processing integrity criterion does it support?",
 "PI1.4, outputs", ["PI1.2, inputs", "PI1.3, processing", "PI1.1, information specifications"],
 "PI1.4 addresses making available or delivering output completely, accurately and timely, to authorized parties. Inputs and processing are PI1.2 and PI1.3."),
("Under the Trust Services Criteria, processing integrity means system processing is complete, valid, accurate, timely and:",
 "Authorized", ["Encrypted", "Available", "Confidential"],
 "The TSC define processing integrity as processing that is complete, valid, accurate, timely and authorized. Availability and confidentiality are separate categories."),
("A payroll clerk compares the total hours keyed into the system with the total from the timesheets before the run. This control is a:",
 "Batch control total", ["Field-level limit check", "Validity check", "Self-checking digit"],
 "Comparing a total computed from source documents with the total entered detects lost or duplicated input in the batch. A limit check tests each record against a ceiling."),
("An edit rejects any timesheet showing more than 80 hours in a week. This is a:",
 "Limit check", ["Completeness check", "Sequence check", "Self-checking digit"],
 "A limit check compares a field with a preset maximum. A completeness check confirms required fields are filled in."),
("A program flags gaps in the numbering of prenumbered shipping documents. This is a:",
 "Sequence check", ["Reasonableness test", "Field check", "Closed-loop verification"],
 "A sequence check reviews document numbers to find missing or duplicate items. A field check tests that a field holds the right type of character."),
("Two companies' computers exchange purchase orders and invoices in a standard electronic format. This is:",
 "Electronic data interchange", ["Robotic process automation", "Shared services center", "Business process outsourcing"],
 "EDI is the computer-to-computer exchange of business documents in a standard format. RPA automates tasks within a user's own screens."),
("A company moves its payroll processing to an outside provider to cut cost. This change is an example of:",
 "Business process outsourcing", ["Robotic process automation", "Vertical integration", "Parallel system conversion"],
 "Handing a whole process to a third party is outsourcing. The company still owns the controls it relies on, which is why it asks for the provider's SOC 1 report."),
("After a nightly batch job, the number of records processed is reconciled to the number received. Which processing integrity area does this address?",
 "Completeness of processing", ["Authorization of inputs", "Distribution of outputs", "Retention of stored data"],
 "Record counts in and out show whether every accepted record was processed, which is PI1.3. It does not show who authorized the input."),
("A walkthrough of cash collections shows one clerk opens the mail and also posts customer payments to the receivables ledger. The main risk is:",
 "Lapping of customer receipts", ["Late shipment of customer orders", "Duplicate payments to vendors", "Overstated inventory counts"],
 "A clerk who handles cash and records it can steal a payment and cover it with later customers' receipts. Shipping, vendor payments and inventory sit in other cycles."),
]
